<onlyinclude>An '''emergent algorithm''' is an informal term for a computational procedure in which coordinated large-scale behavior arises from interactions among local rules or components, rather than being specified as a centralized sequence of every global action.

== Explanation ==
A flocking simulation can generate a coherent moving group even though each simulated individual responds only to nearby individuals. Designers specify the local rules, while the resulting global behavior is studied or exploited. The term does not imply that the procedure was created without design.

